  "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
